# Content copy

User-facing text (UI, `app/data/*`, meta titles, case blurbs) must read like a person wrote it. No AI typography tells.

## Forbidden in site copy

- Em dash `—` and en dash `–` (use ASCII hyphen `-`, comma, or parentheses)
- Guillemets `« »` (use straight double quotes `"`)
- Angle brackets as decoration or fake tags (`<word>`, `<<...>>`)
- Decorative arrows `→` `←` `⇒` in prose (use "to", "then", or `-`)
- Ellipsis character `…` (use `...`)
- Emoji checkmarks / crosses in product copy

## Preferred

```text
BAD:  SaaS platforms—architecture, delivery, and production.
GOOD: SaaS platforms: architecture, delivery, and production.

BAD:  Nov 2025 – Jul 2026
GOOD: Nov 2025 - Jul 2026

BAD:  «also built»
GOOD: "also built"

BAD:  Built → Designed
GOOD: Built, then Designed
```

## Scope

- Applies to: page UI, `profile.ts` / other data shown on the site, `title` / `description`, README blurbs that describe the live site
- Does not rewrite third-party titles you must quote exactly (e.g. a Dribbble shot name); prefer paraphrase when possible
- Internal planning docs may stay casual, but prefer the same hygiene so examples stay consistent

When generating or editing copy, strip these artifacts before finishing.
